<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saffron Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2007">2007</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saffron Revolution was a wave of protests in Myanmar in August–October 2007, named after the robes of the Buddhist monks who led them. Sparked by a sharp rise in fuel prices, the marches grew to tens of thousands in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Yangon</a> and other cities before the military government crushed them in late September, raiding monasteries and killing dozens of people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saffron-revolution.jpg" alt="Saffron Revolution" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: racoles · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2007_Myanmar_protests_7.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
